The gravitational force of attraction between two bodies is directly proportional to the product of their masses.

It is also inversely proportional to the square of the distance between them.

F = G (m₁m₂/r²)

Where F is the force between the masses;


• G is the gravitational constant (6.674×10−¹¹ N · (m/kg)²);

• m₁ is the first mass;

• m₂ is the second mass;

• r is the distance between the centers of the masses.
